# 2. New Terms

The following terms are introduced by this specification. They have been added to the System Context and Domain Glossary (current version v1.9) via the v1.8 amendment.

| **Term** | **Definition** |
| --- | --- |
| **In-application notification** | A system-generated message delivered to a specific OBS user's notification inbox within the OBS application. Generated by defined workflow events. Persisted in obs.notifications. |
| **Notification inbox** | The panel displayed when a user activates the notification bell. Lists the user's in-application notifications in reverse chronological order. Accessible from any authenticated screen via the notification bell in the application shell header. |
| **Unread count** | The count of in-application notifications for the authenticated user where is_read = FALSE. Displayed as a badge on the notification bell icon in the application shell header. |

# 3. Notification Bell — Application Shell Integration

The notification bell is a persistent element of the application shell header. It is visible on every authenticated screen to all authenticated users.

## 3.1 Placement

| **Decision: ****The notification bell icon is placed in the application shell header bar, to the left of the user identity section at the top of the left sidebar. On desktop, it renders as an icon button (MUI IconButton with NotificationsNone or Notifications icon) positioned in the top-right area of the sidebar, above the user identity block. On tablet and mobile, it renders in the same relative position within the collapsed or drawer sidebar. The bell is always visible regardless of which module is active.** |
| --- |

## 3.2 Unread Count Badge

When the authenticated user has one or more unread notifications (is_read = FALSE), a numeric badge is displayed on the notification bell icon. Badge behaviour:

- Badge is rendered using MUI Badge with the unread_count value.

- When unread_count = 0, the badge is not rendered — the bell icon is shown without a badge.

- When unread_count > 99, the badge displays '99+'.

- The unread count is fetched from GET /api/v1/notifications?unread_only=true at session load and refreshed by polling GET /api/v1/notifications every 60 seconds while the user's session is active. The polling interval is configurable via an environment variable NOTIFICATION_POLL_INTERVAL_SECONDS; default 60.

- On successful mark-read or mark-all-read operations, the badge count is updated immediately in the frontend without waiting for the next polling cycle.

| **Claude Code Note — Notification bell implementation** | **Component: src/components/layout/NotificationBell.tsx Place in AppShell.tsx above the user identity block in the sidebar. Use MUI Badge wrapping MUI IconButton with Notifications icon (filled when unread ****>**** 0, NotificationsNone when unread = 0). Polling implementation:   useEffect with setInterval — interval set to NOTIFICATION_POLL_INTERVAL_SECONDS * 1000.   Call GET /api/v1/notifications?unread_only=true****&****page_size=1 to retrieve unread_count only.   On tab visibility change (document.visibilityState === ****'****hidden****'****), pause polling.   Resume polling when tab becomes visible — immediately fetch on resume.   Clear interval on component unmount. Store unread count in React state within NotificationBell component. Do NOT store notifications in ObsUserContext — context is for identity/permissions only. On successful mark-all-read: immediately set local unread count state to 0. On successful mark-one-read: decrement local unread count state by 1 (floor 0).** |
| --- | --- |

## 3.3 Notification Inbox Panel

Clicking the notification bell opens the notification inbox panel. The inbox panel is a non-blocking overlay (not a full-page navigation) that displays above the main content area.

### 3.3.1 Panel Layout

The inbox panel is implemented as a MUI Popover anchored to the notification bell icon. Panel dimensions: 400px wide on desktop; full-width drawer on mobile. Height: up to 600px with internal scroll; shorter if fewer items. Panel structure from top to bottom:

- **Panel header** — title 'Notifications' (bold, 16pt); a 'Mark all as read' text button (right-aligned, disabled when unread_count = 0).

- **Notification list** — scrollable list of notification items (Section 3.3.2), most recent first.

- **Panel footer** — 'View all' link (if total_count exceeds the displayed page size) — navigates to a dedicated /notifications full-page view. If total_count <= page_size, no footer is shown.

Closing the panel: clicking outside the panel (Popover onClose), pressing Escape, or clicking the bell icon again closes the panel. Closing does not mark any notifications as read.

| **Claude Code Note — Notification inbox panel implementation** | **Component: src/components/layout/NotificationInbox.tsx Render as MUI Popover anchored to the notification bell button. On open: call GET /api/v1/notifications?page_size=20****&****unread_only=false to load initial list. Display MUI CircularProgress while loading. On load error: display ****'****Unable to load notifications. Please try again.****'**** with retry link. List implementation: MUI List with MUI ListItem per notification. The full-page /notifications route renders the same NotificationInbox content but paginated (page_size=50) and within the main content area layout.** |
| --- | --- |

### 3.3.2 Notification Item Rendering

Each notification item in the list displays:

- A filled circle indicator (8px, theme primary colour) on the left when is_read = FALSE. No indicator when is_read = TRUE.

- Notification title (bold when unread, normal weight when read).

- Notification body text — truncated to two lines with ellipsis in the list view.

- Relative timestamp — e.g., 'Just now', '5 minutes ago', '2 hours ago', 'Yesterday', or a date for older items.

- The entire item is clickable. On click: (1) call POST /api/v1/notifications/{notification_id}/mark-read; (2) if deep_link_url is set, navigate to that URL within OBS; (3) close the inbox panel.

- A secondary 'Mark as read' action (MUI icon button, DoneAll icon) is shown on hover for unread items. Clicking this marks the item read without navigating.

### 3.3.3 Empty State

When the user has no notifications (total_count = 0): display a centred message — 'No notifications yet.' with a secondary line 'You will be notified here when action is required or when updates affect your cost centers.'

# 4. Notification Events

The following table defines all notification events, their recipients, message content, and implementation notes. Notifications are generated server-side by the API handler that processes the triggering event — never by the frontend. All message content is pre-formatted and stored in obs.notifications at write time.

| **Trigger Event** | **Recipient(s)** | **Notification Message** | **Implementation Notes** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| TRANSFER_INITIATED | Designated transfer approver of receiving cost center | Transfer request received: [Position Title] from [Sending Cost Center Name] requested by [Initiator Display Name]. Effective date: [effective_date]. Expires in 3 days. | Links to the transfer approval action in the Workforce Planning module. Recipient is the transfer_approver_user_id configured on the receiving cost center. |
| TRANSFER_REJECTED | The user identified by initiated_by on the transfer record | Your transfer request for [Position Title] to [Receiving Cost Center Name] was rejected by [Approver Display Name]. | Links to the position in the Workforce Planning module. |
| TRANSFER_EXPIRED | The user identified by initiated_by on the transfer record | Your transfer request for [Position Title] to [Receiving Cost Center Name] has expired with no action taken. The position remains in [Sending Cost Center Name]. | Links to the position in the Workforce Planning module. Generated by the 3-day expiry background job. |
| BUDGET_SUBMITTED | Finance Reviewers whose assigned cost center scope includes the submitted cost_center_id | [Cost Center Name] — FY[Year] ([Version Name]) has been submitted for Finance review by [Submitter Display Name]. | Links to the Finance Review module Review Detail screen. Recipients resolved by querying obs.user_cost_center_grants and obs.user_rollup_grants for users with is_finance_reviewer = TRUE. |
| BUDGET_APPROVED | The user identified by submitted_by on the finance review record | Your budget for [Cost Center Name] — FY[Year] ([Version Name]) has been approved by [Reviewer Display Name]. Reason: [approval_reason, truncated to 300 chars if longer]. | Links to the Budget Planning module for the cost center. |
| BUDGET_REJECTED | The user identified by submitted_by on the finance review record | Your budget for [Cost Center Name] — FY[Year] ([Version Name]) has been rejected by [Reviewer Display Name]. Reason: [rejection_reason, truncated to 300 chars if longer]. Please revise and resubmit. | Links to the Budget Planning module for the cost center. |
| BUDGET_VERSION_APPROVED | All Administrators (is_administrator = TRUE) | Budget version [Version Name] — FY[Year] is fully approved. All submitted cost centers have been approved by Finance. | Links to the Budget Versions administration screen. |
| BUDGET_VERSION_REJECTED | All Administrators (is_administrator = TRUE) | Budget version [Version Name] — FY[Year] has been rejected. One or more cost center submissions were rejected by Finance. | Links to the Budget Versions administration screen. |

## 4.1 Recipient Resolution

Recipient resolution rules by event type:

- **TRANSFER_INITIATED:** the single user identified by the receiving cost center's transfer_approver_user_id field in obs.cost_center_configuration. One notification record is created.

- **TRANSFER_REJECTED and TRANSFER_EXPIRED:** the single user identified by obs.position_transfers.initiated_by. One notification record is created.

- **BUDGET_SUBMITTED:** all users where is_finance_reviewer = TRUE and who have a cost center grant (via obs.user_cost_center_grants or obs.user_rollup_grants) covering the submitted cost_center_id. One notification record per qualifying Finance Reviewer.

- **BUDGET_APPROVED and BUDGET_REJECTED:** the single user identified by obs.finance_review_records.submitted_by. One notification record is created.

- **BUDGET_VERSION_APPROVED and BUDGET_VERSION_REJECTED:** all users where is_administrator = TRUE. One notification record per Administrator.

## 4.2 Notification Generation — Server-Side Rules

| **Decision: ****Notifications are generated synchronously within the same API transaction as the triggering event. If notification creation fails, it must not roll back the triggering event — notification failure is non-fatal. Log a WARNING-level error for any notification write failure. The triggering event****'****s audit log entry is written regardless of notification outcome.** |
| --- |

| **Claude Code Note — Notification service implementation** | **Module: src/services/notification_service.py Function: create_notification(user_id, event_type, title, body, deep_link_url,           source_entity_type, source_entity_id, expires_at=None)   INSERT INTO obs.notifications (     notification_id, user_id, event_type, title, body, deep_link_url, is_read,     source_entity_type, source_entity_id, created_at, expires_at)   VALUES (uuid(), :user_id, :event_type, :title, :body, :deep_link_url, FALSE,           :source_entity_type, :source_entity_id, NOW(), :expires_at); Function: create_notifications_bulk(recipients: list[user_id], ...same args...)   Used for BUDGET_SUBMITTED (multiple Finance Reviewer recipients) and   BUDGET_VERSION_APPROVED / BUDGET_VERSION_REJECTED (all Administrators).   Insert one obs.notifications record per recipient in a single batch INSERT. Wrap all create_notification calls in try/except. On exception: log WARNING with event_type, entity_id, and error — do not re-raise. The triggering API handler must not be affected by notification write failures. Integration points — add create_notification call to these existing API handlers:   POST /api/v1/positions/{position_id}/transfer     -****>**** create_notification(transfer_approver_user_id, ****'****TRANSFER_INITIATED****'****, ...)   POST /api/v1/transfers/{transfer_id}/reject     -****>**** create_notification(initiated_by, ****'****TRANSFER_REJECTED****'****, ...)   Background job: transfer expiry processor     -****>**** create_notification(initiated_by, ****'****TRANSFER_EXPIRED****'****, ...) per expired transfer   POST /api/v1/budget-versions/{version_id}/submit     -****>**** create_notifications_bulk(finance_reviewer_recipients, ****'****BUDGET_SUBMITTED****'****, ...)   POST /api/v1/finance-review/{review_id}/approve     -****>**** create_notification(submitted_by, ****'****BUDGET_APPROVED****'****, ...)   POST /api/v1/finance-review/{review_id}/reject     -****>**** create_notification(submitted_by, ****'****BUDGET_REJECTED****'****, ...)   resolve_budget_version_status() — on version transition to Approved:     -****>**** create_notifications_bulk(all_administrators, ****'****BUDGET_VERSION_APPROVED****'****, ...)   resolve_budget_version_status() — on version transition to Rejected:     -****>**** create_notifications_bulk(all_administrators, ****'****BUDGET_VERSION_REJECTED****'****, ...)** |
| --- | --- |

## 4.3 Transfer Request Notification Expiry

A TRANSFER_INITIATED notification sent to the designated transfer approver expires when the associated transfer record is no longer pending. This prevents stale action prompts in the approver's inbox.

- When a transfer request is approved, rejected, or expires (status transitions out of 'pending'), the corresponding TRANSFER_INITIATED notification for that transfer_id is expired: UPDATE obs.notifications SET expires_at = NOW() WHERE source_entity_id = :transfer_id AND event_type = 'TRANSFER_INITIATED'.

- Expired notifications (expires_at IS NOT NULL AND expires_at < NOW()) are excluded from GET /api/v1/notifications responses.

- Expired notifications are retained in obs.notifications for audit purposes — they are never deleted.

# 5. Deep-Link Routing

Each notification event type maps to a deep-link URL within OBS. The deep_link_url field is a relative path stored in the notification record at write time.

| **Event Type** | **deep_link_url pattern** |
| --- | --- |
| TRANSFER_INITIATED | /workforce-planning/{receiving_cost_center_id}/positions/{position_id}?action=review-transfer&transfer_id={transfer_id} |
| TRANSFER_REJECTED | /workforce-planning/{sending_cost_center_id}/positions/{position_id} |
| TRANSFER_EXPIRED | /workforce-planning/{sending_cost_center_id}/positions/{position_id} |
| BUDGET_SUBMITTED | /finance-review/{review_id} |
| BUDGET_APPROVED | /budget-planning/{cost_center_id}?version_id={version_id}&fiscal_year={fiscal_year} |
| BUDGET_REJECTED | /budget-planning/{cost_center_id}?version_id={version_id}&fiscal_year={fiscal_year} |
| BUDGET_VERSION_APPROVED | /administration/budget-versions?version_id={version_id} |
| BUDGET_VERSION_REJECTED | /administration/budget-versions?version_id={version_id} |

Deep-link navigation behaviour: when a user clicks a notification with a deep_link_url, the frontend uses React Router's navigate() to route to the URL. If the user does not have access to the target (e.g., they have since lost a cost center grant), the target screen renders its standard HTTP 403 access denied state — the notification system does not pre-validate access before navigating.

# 6. Access Control

All notification API endpoints enforce user-scoped access server-side. The frontend reflects these rules but the API is the authoritative enforcement point.

| **Action** | **Standard User** | **Finance Reviewer** | **Administrator** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| View notification bell (header) | All authenticated users | All authenticated users | All authenticated users |
| See unread count badge | All authenticated users (own count only) | All authenticated users (own count only) | All authenticated users (own count only) |
| View inbox panel | All authenticated users (own notifications only) | All authenticated users (own notifications only) | All authenticated users (own notifications only) |
| Mark individual notification read | Own notifications only — HTTP 403 for other users' notifications | Own notifications only | Own notifications only |
| Mark all read | Own notifications only | Own notifications only | Own notifications only |
| Receive transfer request notification | Yes — if designated transfer approver | No | Yes — implicit |
| Receive transfer rejected/expired notification | Yes — if transfer initiator | No | Yes — if initiator |
| Receive budget submission notification | No — unless also is_finance_reviewer | Yes — for assigned cost centers | Yes — for all cost centers |
| Receive budget approved/rejected notification | Yes — if they submitted the budget | Yes — if they submitted the budget | Yes — if they submitted the budget |
| Receive version approved/rejected notification | No | No | Yes — all Administrators |

| **Claude Code Note — Notification API access control** | **GET /api/v1/notifications:   WHERE user_id = :authenticated_user_id  -- always inject, never accept user_id as query param   AND (expires_at IS NULL OR expires_at ****>**** NOW())   ORDER BY created_at DESC   LIMIT :page_size OFFSET (:page - 1) * :page_size POST /api/v1/notifications/{notification_id}/mark-read:   SELECT user_id FROM obs.notifications WHERE notification_id = :id   IF user_id != authenticated_user_id: return HTTP 403   UPDATE obs.notifications SET is_read = TRUE, read_at = NOW()   WHERE notification_id = :id AND user_id = :authenticated_user_id   Write NOTIFICATION_READ audit event: notification_id, user_id, timestamp POST /api/v1/notifications/mark-all-read:   UPDATE obs.notifications SET is_read = TRUE, read_at = NOW()   WHERE user_id = :authenticated_user_id AND is_read = FALSE   Return { marked_read_count: rowcount }   Write NOTIFICATION_READ audit event with entity_id = ****'****all****'** |
| --- | --- |

# 7. PostgreSQL Schema

## 7.1 obs.notifications Table

| **Column** | **Type** | **Description** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **notification_id** | STRING NOT NULL | Generated UUID. Primary key. |
| **user_id** | STRING NOT NULL | FK to obs.users. The recipient of the notification. |
| **event_type** | STRING NOT NULL | The audit event that triggered this notification (e.g., TRANSFER_INITIATED, BUDGET_APPROVED). Must match a value in the audit event type enumeration. |
| **title** | STRING NOT NULL | Short notification title derived from the event. Maximum 200 characters. Pre-formatted at write time. |
| **body** | STRING NOT NULL | Full notification message body. Maximum 1,000 characters. Pre-formatted at write time with resolved display names and entity labels. |
| **deep_link_url** | STRING (nullable) | Relative URL within OBS for the notification action target. Null if no direct link target. |
| **is_read** | BOOLEAN NOT NULL | DEFAULT FALSE. Set to TRUE when the user marks the notification read. |
| **read_at** | TIMESTAMP (nullable) | UTC timestamp when the notification was marked read. Null if unread. |
| **source_entity_type** | STRING NOT NULL | The type of entity that generated the notification (e.g., PositionTransfer, FinanceReviewRecord, BudgetVersion). |
| **source_entity_id** | STRING NOT NULL | The ID of the source entity (transfer_id, review_id, version_id, etc.). |
| **created_at** | TIMESTAMP NOT NULL | UTC timestamp when the notification record was created. Set to the event timestamp of the triggering audit event. |
| **expires_at** | TIMESTAMP (nullable) | Optional expiry. If set and expires_at < NOW(), the notification is excluded from inbox queries. Use for time-bounded notifications (e.g., transfer requests). Transfer request notifications expire when the transfer record reaches 'approved', 'rejected', or 'expired' status. |

| **Claude Code Note — obs.notifications DDL** | **CREATE TABLE obs.notifications (   notification_id        STRING NOT NULL,   user_id                STRING NOT NULL,   event_type             STRING NOT NULL,   title                  STRING NOT NULL,   body                   STRING NOT NULL,   deep_link_url          STRING,   is_read                BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE,   read_at                TIMESTAMP,   source_entity_type     STRING NOT NULL,   source_entity_id       STRING NOT NULL,   created_at             TIMESTAMP NOT NULL,   expires_at             TIMESTAMP ); Index for per-user query optimisation:   CREATE INDEX idx_notifications_user_unread_created     ON obs.notifications (user_id, is_read, created_at DESC); Retention: notification records are retained indefinitely. Expired records (expires_at ****<**** NOW()) are excluded at query time, not deleted. NOTE: obs.notifications is NOT an audit log. It is a mutable user-facing table. is_read and read_at are the only mutable columns — all other columns are immutable once the record is created. Audit events for read actions are written to obs.audit_log separately (NOTIFICATION_READ event).** |
| --- | --- |

## 7.2 Audit Event

One new audit event type is introduced by this specification:

| **Event Type** | **Payload Fields** |
| --- | --- |
| **NOTIFICATION_READ** | notification_id (or 'all' for mark-all-read), user_id, timestamp. Written when a user marks one or all notifications as read. |

# 8. Notification Service API

All endpoints conform to the RESTful API patterns established in Application Architecture Specification v3.6. All endpoints require a valid Entra ID access token.

| **Endpoint** | **Specification** |
| --- | --- |
| **GET /api/v1/notifications** | Returns the authenticated user's notifications. Query parameters: unread_only BOOLEAN (default false); page INT (default 1); page_size INT (default 20, max 50). Response HTTP 200: { unread_count: int, total_count: int, page: int, page_size: int, notifications: [ { notification_id, event_type, title, body, deep_link_url, is_read, read_at, source_entity_type, source_entity_id, created_at, expires_at } ] }. Scope: server enforces user_id = authenticated user — no cross-user reads. |
| **POST /api/v1/notifications/{notification_id}/mark-read** | Marks a single notification as read for the authenticated user. Validates notification_id belongs to the authenticated user — HTTP 403 if not. On success: UPDATE obs.notifications SET is_read = TRUE, read_at = NOW() WHERE notification_id = :id AND user_id = :user_id. Returns HTTP 200 with updated notification record. Idempotent — marking an already-read notification returns HTTP 200 with no state change. |
| **POST /api/v1/notifications/mark-all-read** | Marks all unread notifications as read for the authenticated user. UPDATE obs.notifications SET is_read = TRUE, read_at = NOW() WHERE user_id = :user_id AND is_read = FALSE. Returns HTTP 200: { marked_read_count: int }. |

## 8.1 Non-Functional Requirements

| **Requirement** | **Target** | **Notes** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Notification bell unread count load | < 500ms | First load at session start. Polling should not degrade perceived performance. |
| Notification inbox panel open | < 1 second for first 20 items | Fetch triggered on panel open. |
| Mark-read response | < 300ms | Must feel instantaneous — update badge optimistically. |
| Maximum notifications per user | No hard cap; query always paginated | Use the (user_id, is_read, created_at DESC) index for efficient per-user queries. |

