# 10. Acceptance Criteria

Each criterion below is independently testable. Server-side enforcement is verified at the API layer.

## 10.1 Notification Bell and Badge

| **ID** | **Criterion** |
| --- | --- |
| **AC-NOTIF-BELL-01** | The notification bell icon is rendered in the application shell header on every authenticated screen, for all authenticated users. |
| **AC-NOTIF-BELL-02** | When the authenticated user has zero unread notifications, the notification bell is rendered without a badge. |
| **AC-NOTIF-BELL-03** | When the authenticated user has one or more unread notifications, a numeric badge displays the unread_count on the notification bell. |
| **AC-NOTIF-BELL-04** | When unread_count > 99, the badge displays '99+'. |
| **AC-NOTIF-BELL-05** | The unread count is polled from GET /api/v1/notifications at the configured interval (default 60 seconds). The badge updates without a page reload. |
| **AC-NOTIF-BELL-06** | Polling pauses when the browser tab loses visibility and resumes — with an immediate fetch — when the tab regains visibility. |

## 10.2 Notification Inbox Panel

| **ID** | **Criterion** |
| --- | --- |
| **AC-NOTIF-INB-01** | Clicking the notification bell opens the inbox panel. Clicking it again, or clicking outside the panel, or pressing Escape closes the panel. |
| **AC-NOTIF-INB-02** | The inbox panel displays the authenticated user's notifications in reverse chronological order (most recent first). |
| **AC-NOTIF-INB-03** | Unread notifications are visually distinguished from read notifications (filled indicator, bold title). |
| **AC-NOTIF-INB-04** | Clicking a notification item calls POST /api/v1/notifications/{notification_id}/mark-read and navigates to the deep_link_url if one is set. The panel closes on click. |
| **AC-NOTIF-INB-05** | Clicking 'Mark as read' on a notification item calls POST /api/v1/notifications/{notification_id}/mark-read without navigating. The badge count decrements by 1. |
| **AC-NOTIF-INB-06** | Clicking 'Mark all as read' calls POST /api/v1/notifications/mark-all-read. All items in the panel transition to read state. The badge count is set to 0. |
| **AC-NOTIF-INB-07** | 'Mark all as read' is disabled when unread_count = 0. |
| **AC-NOTIF-INB-08** | When the user has no notifications, the empty state message is displayed. |
| **AC-NOTIF-INB-09** | Expired notifications (expires_at < NOW()) are not displayed in the inbox panel. |

## 10.3 Notification API

| **ID** | **Criterion** |
| --- | --- |
| **AC-NOTIF-API-01** | GET /api/v1/notifications returns only the authenticated user's own notifications. Attempting to retrieve another user's notifications is not possible via this endpoint — user_id is always resolved from the access token. |
| **AC-NOTIF-API-02** | GET /api/v1/notifications with unread_only=true returns only records with is_read = FALSE. |
| **AC-NOTIF-API-03** | GET /api/v1/notifications excludes notifications where expires_at IS NOT NULL AND expires_at < NOW(). |
| **AC-NOTIF-API-04** | POST /api/v1/notifications/{notification_id}/mark-read returns HTTP 403 when the notification_id does not belong to the authenticated user. |
| **AC-NOTIF-API-05** | POST /api/v1/notifications/{notification_id}/mark-read on an already-read notification returns HTTP 200 with no state change (idempotent). |
| **AC-NOTIF-API-06** | POST /api/v1/notifications/mark-all-read returns { marked_read_count: N } where N is the number of records updated. |
| **AC-NOTIF-API-07** | An unauthenticated request to any notification endpoint returns HTTP 401. |

## 10.4 Notification Delivery — Workforce Planning Events

| **ID** | **Criterion** |
| --- | --- |
| **AC-NOTIF-WP-01** | Initiating a transfer via POST /api/v1/positions/{position_id}/transfer creates an obs.notifications record for the designated transfer approver of the receiving cost center with event_type = 'TRANSFER_INITIATED'. |
| **AC-NOTIF-WP-02** | The TRANSFER_INITIATED notification includes a deep_link_url referencing the transfer approval action in the Workforce Planning module. |
| **AC-NOTIF-WP-03** | Rejecting a transfer via POST /api/v1/transfers/{transfer_id}/reject creates an obs.notifications record for the transfer initiating user with event_type = 'TRANSFER_REJECTED'. |
| **AC-NOTIF-WP-04** | When the transfer expiry background job sets a transfer to 'expired', it creates an obs.notifications record for the transfer initiating user with event_type = 'TRANSFER_EXPIRED'. |
| **AC-NOTIF-WP-05** | When a transfer transitions out of 'pending' status (approved, rejected, or expired), the corresponding TRANSFER_INITIATED notification for that transfer_id has its expires_at set to NOW(), causing it to no longer appear in the approver's inbox. |
| **AC-NOTIF-WP-06** | If notification creation fails (e.g., database write error), the triggering transfer API operation succeeds and returns its normal HTTP 200 response. The notification failure is logged as a WARNING but does not roll back or fail the transfer action. |

## 10.5 Notification Delivery — Finance Approval Workflow Events

| **ID** | **Criterion** |
| --- | --- |
| **AC-NOTIF-FAW-01** | A successful call to POST /api/v1/budget-versions/{version_id}/submit creates one obs.notifications record for each Finance Reviewer whose assigned cost center scope includes the submitted cost_center_id. |
| **AC-NOTIF-FAW-02** | A successful call to POST /api/v1/finance-review/{review_id}/approve creates one obs.notifications record for the user identified by obs.finance_review_records.submitted_by with event_type = 'BUDGET_APPROVED'. |
| **AC-NOTIF-FAW-03** | A successful call to POST /api/v1/finance-review/{review_id}/reject creates one obs.notifications record for the user identified by obs.finance_review_records.submitted_by with event_type = 'BUDGET_REJECTED'. |
| **AC-NOTIF-FAW-04** | When resolve_budget_version_status() transitions a budget version to 'Approved', one obs.notifications record is created for each user where is_administrator = TRUE with event_type = 'BUDGET_VERSION_APPROVED'. |
| **AC-NOTIF-FAW-05** | When resolve_budget_version_status() transitions a budget version to 'Rejected', one obs.notifications record is created for each user where is_administrator = TRUE with event_type = 'BUDGET_VERSION_REJECTED'. |
| **AC-NOTIF-FAW-06** | If notification creation fails for any FAW event, the triggering API operation succeeds and returns its normal HTTP response. The notification failure is logged as a WARNING and does not roll back the FAW action. |

## 10.6 obs.notifications Schema

| **ID** | **Criterion** |
| --- | --- |
| **AC-NOTIF-SCH-01** | The obs.notifications PostgreSQL table exists with all columns defined in Section 7.1, together with the (user_id, is_read, created_at DESC) index. |
| **AC-NOTIF-SCH-02** | notification_id, user_id, event_type, title, body, source_entity_type, source_entity_id, and created_at are never null. |
| **AC-NOTIF-SCH-03** | Newly created notification records have is_read = FALSE and read_at = NULL. |
| **AC-NOTIF-SCH-04** | After a mark-read operation, the record has is_read = TRUE and read_at set to a non-null UTC timestamp. |
| **AC-NOTIF-SCH-05** | Expired notifications (expires_at IS NOT NULL AND expires_at < NOW()) are retained in the table and are not deleted. They are excluded at query time only. |

